meta {
  name: Toggle Technique Status
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

patch {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/incidents/custom-technique/:techniqueId/toggle
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 4
  techniqueId: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Toggle Custom Technique Active Status

  Toggles the active/inactive status of a custom intervention technique.
  Inactive techniques will not appear in the dropdown options.

  ## Path Parameters:
  - `house` - House ID
  - `youngPersonId` - Young person ID
  - `techniqueId` - The ID of the custom technique to toggle

  ## Authorization:
  Must have `update_incident` permission.

  ## Behavior:
  - If technique is currently active → sets to inactive
  - If technique is currently inactive → sets to active
  - Inactive techniques are hidden from GET /method-technique-options

  ## Response Success:
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Technique status updated successfully",
    "data": null
  }
  ```

  ## Response Error:
  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "message": "Technique not found or unauthorized",
    "data": null
  }
  ```

  ## Use Cases:
  - Temporarily disable a technique without deleting it
  - Reactivate a previously disabled technique
  - Manage which custom techniques are available to staff

  ## Notes:
  - Only affects custom techniques (built-in options are always active)
  - User must have access to the house or client that owns the technique
  - Status change is immediate and affects all future dropdown loads
}
